ocol is also complete on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered data and service state, and successful post-restart authentication were captured. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor's observations.","limitations":["Secret and password values were appropriately redacted, so their literal contents cannot be independently compared; length, placement, synchronization, and live authentication behavior were directly verified.","The captured wrong-secret outputs summarize command assertions rather than displaying the raw radtest response, although both tests explicitly checked that Access-Accept was absent and returned a failing client status.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory all configuration paths, so retained .pre-legacy2 backup files are inferred from their creation commands rather than independently enumerated; they appear to be bounded rollback backups rather than harmful residue."]}
